    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "ff16a53e-f7b1-31ea-bc9c-dff1e264d9a2",
                "word": "salacity",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "49b1bdf8-62cb-47bd-b871-d67cda15c18c",
                        "entry_id": "ff16a53e-f7b1-31ea-bc9c-dff1e264d9a2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "salacities"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34b9164a-0149-3393-a64f-8d29e19f9a2b",
                        "entry_id": "ff16a53e-f7b1-31ea-bc9c-dff1e264d9a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state or quality of being salacious; lewdness, obscenity, bawdiness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1cd1ec77-9934-4f88-a765-6cdc422697fb",
                                "sense_id": "34b9164a-0149-3393-a64f-8d29e19f9a2b",
                                "text": "One of the males is sufficient in procreation for seuen or nine of the females, and by that means they are made more fruitful, but if you put them one male to one femal, then will the venereous salacity of the male procure abortment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae453ab6-d471-4866-b129-eba57932142f",
                                "sense_id": "34b9164a-0149-3393-a64f-8d29e19f9a2b",
                                "text": "Aristotle gives instance in sparrows, which are parum vivaces ob salacitatem, short-lived because of their salacity, which is very frequent […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62996907-ca95-4425-932c-47e4a12032b1",
                                "sense_id": "34b9164a-0149-3393-a64f-8d29e19f9a2b",
                                "text": "The Portugueze, tho’ eminently abſtemious and temperate in all other Things, are unbounded in their Luſts; and perhaps they ſubſtitute the former in room of a Surgeon, as a Counterpoiſon to the Miſchiefs of a promiſcuous Salacity: They have moſt of them Venereal Taints, and with Age become meager and hectick: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66c00ecc-1528-43d0-87e3-69116e2c69f1",
                                "sense_id": "34b9164a-0149-3393-a64f-8d29e19f9a2b",
                                "text": "She had had no experience with this class of individuals whatsoever, and did not know the salacity and humour of the theatrical tribe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2cdb09a-cc53-4f8d-9f76-da07a9f50b6e",
                                "sense_id": "34b9164a-0149-3393-a64f-8d29e19f9a2b",
                                "text": "Although it would have been allowed, I did not keep a journal over those six months. From the start I saw that what I wanted to say, although ‘hereafter, in a better world than this’ it might find other readers and do its good, would have brought nothing but scorn and salacity at the time."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "302e3752-6a9c-3e8f-b15a-bf9f4df9a59b",
                        "entry_id": "ff16a53e-f7b1-31ea-bc9c-dff1e264d9a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An act that is salacious, (lewd, obscene or bawdy); a salacious image or piece of writing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "09f4acc5-f741-4d4e-b46a-ba9938e9bb10",
                                "sense_id": "302e3752-6a9c-3e8f-b15a-bf9f4df9a59b",
                                "text": "The editors of the Unitarian New Version of the New Testament, who very modestly wish to shovel all these spurcities and salacities out of the sacred text, have the impudence to tell us, in a note, that they were interpolated to lessen the odium attached to Christianity […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ee04717-56f6-4880-b853-5928ade349f7",
                                "sense_id": "302e3752-6a9c-3e8f-b15a-bf9f4df9a59b",
                                "text": "[…] from the hilltop were to be seen no cluttered barren lots sodden with spring rain and churned and torn by hoof of horse and cattle, no piles of winter ashes and rusting tin cans, no dingy hoardings covered with the tattered insanities of posted salacities and advertisements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c944d012-2f90-4acd-911a-c51f44131686",
                                "sense_id": "302e3752-6a9c-3e8f-b15a-bf9f4df9a59b",
                                "text": "Sartre decrees that Gustave was never homosexual; merely passive and feminine in his psychology. The byplay with Bouilhet was just teasing, the outer edge of vivid male friendship: Gustave never committed a single homosexual act in all his life. He says he did, but that was boastful invention: Bouilhet asked for salacities from Cairo, and Flaubert provided them [in his letters]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "83afd29f-5791-40f1-a828-6bebe6588d87",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff16a53e-f7b1-31ea-bc9c-dff1e264d9a2",
                        "source_sense_description": "the state or quality of being salacious",
                        "target_lang_word": "salacité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "salacité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b944dba-b9bf-3241-82ae-d990165e5e84",
                                        "entry_id": "e52fed3c-2cbd-34b4-9b63-5ea73e48a2b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Penchant prononcé pour l’érotisme, l’obscénité, les rapports sexuels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcf3e63f-9dc0-48b1-a873-60340b04a041",
                                                "sense_id": "4b944dba-b9bf-3241-82ae-d990165e5e84",
                                                "text": "Le plus souvent, sans doute, c’est dans un moment d’ébriété ou plutôt de cette salacité irrésistible, que déchaîne dans le sang de l’Européen l’air balsamique et chaud des tropiques, que le baiser criminel aura rapproché du maître la sémillante esclave, aux formes exubérantes et gracieuses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f22c301-9672-44f5-9023-01366765d0b1",
                                                "sense_id": "4b944dba-b9bf-3241-82ae-d990165e5e84",
                                                "text": "Les couleurs tranchées de sa cotte hardie amusent l’œil, et elle peut découvrir jusqu’aux jarretières, ou peu s’en faut, une jambe fine moulée dans un bas rouge à coins d’or, perspective agréable aux jeunes comme aux vieux, aux vieux surtout dont elle réveille la salacité endormie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9f1b062-64fb-47f0-9a4f-3ab5a02d44bc",
                                                "sense_id": "4b944dba-b9bf-3241-82ae-d990165e5e84",
                                                "text": "La belle Nicaise était une veuve, fort riche, habitant non loin de la ville et dont la salacité faisait l’objet d’une chronique scandaleuse abondante comme un folklore."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0a349b8-f027-3e0f-bd6d-1aa608c2b98c",
                                        "entry_id": "e52fed3c-2cbd-34b4-9b63-5ea73e48a2b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Caractère érotique, lubrique, obscène de propos ou de comportements."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40b8b18e-0cdc-4004-bd66-c9449fe12768",
                                                "sense_id": "f0a349b8-f027-3e0f-bd6d-1aa608c2b98c",
                                                "text": "Dus en partie à une certaine excitation génésique, ces actes de salacité sont surtout le fait du défaut de conscience et de la perte absolue du sentiment de la pudeur, qui existe chez les déments."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a34656e1-b51c-4207-ac5f-5a63fffd1925",
                                                "sense_id": "f0a349b8-f027-3e0f-bd6d-1aa608c2b98c",
                                                "text": "Il semble que la nature se pervertisse devant lui et que ce soit sa présence même qui la déprave ; pour la première fois, il comprend l’immuable salacité des bois, découvre des priapées dans les futaies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
